generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-352-## Units of analysis and intervals
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-353-
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err:354:- D1/D3: the star is the unit; Wilson 95% intervals on independent per-star
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err:355:  proportions; weighted estimates use the effective-sample-size Wilson
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-356-  approximation.
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err:357:- D2: the TESS target is the CLUSTER. K=3 template windows and ladder/phase
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-358-  variants are correlated replicates, never pooled as independent trials.
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err:359:  Per-stratum (10/50/90th percentile window) proportions are reported
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-360-  separately; aggregates are equal-weight standardized means over targets
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err:361:  with cluster bootstrap intervals (resample targets, keep all replicates;
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-362-  B = 2000, frozen seed). Ladder results: nominal is primary; the min-max
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-363-  across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified finite-grid sensitivity range",
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_abstract.err-364-  never a confidence band; endpoint scenarios identified.
