generalization/reviews/G2/sol_stats2.err-588-    45	   McNemar tests equality of paired marginal detection probabilities, \(P(C=1,L=0)=P(C=0,L=1)\). Strong two-way complementarity can produce \(p=1\), while a significant result can reflect one method simply dominating the other.
