generalization/reviews/G2/sol_stats2.err-611-    68	
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_stats2.err-612-    69	12. **MAJOR — \(n=1000\) is not tied to an acceptance threshold and cannot support the alias audit.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_stats2.err:613:    70	    With zero events, the stated two-sided 95% Wilson upper bound is about 0.38%; that is correct, but only useful if approximately 0.4% is the preregistered acceptable limit. It cannot establish FPR below 0.1%. At an expected alias-blanking rate of 0.03–0.15%, 1,000 nulls yield only 0.3–1.5 expected events, far too few to estimate that rate or an FP frequency distribution.
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_stats2.err-614-    71	
