generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-162-     7	## Numbered objections
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-163-     8	
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:164:     9	1. **REJECT-LEVEL — D2 templates are selected using the pipeline outcome being evaluated.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:165:    10	   The templates are the 510 stars previously classified as “not detected” by the frozen pipeline. That is a direct circularity path: the evaluation conditions the real-noise/window population on the algorithm having failed to trigger. This suppresses trigger-prone artifacts and selects favorable noise realizations. The admission that arm-B nulls are tautological does not cure the bias in positive injection recovery.  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:166:    11	   **Fix:** draw templates without reference to frozen-pipeline status—ideally the actual ZTF windows of the Romero targets, otherwise a prespecified random or weighted sample of the full parent population. Run paired zero-signal and injected versions. If unchanged, every D2 result must explicitly be conditional on “previously non-triggering templates.”
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-167-    12	
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-168-    13	2. **MAJOR — D3 has no obvious ZTF label leakage, but “independently labeled” needs qualification.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-169-    14	   Murphy labels and Mo frequencies are external to the ZTF pipeline, so I see no direct D3 label-to-ZTF-output circularity. However, Mo is described as a Murphy×Bowman-derived sample; these are not independent label sources.  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-170-    15	   **Fix:** say “labels obtained independently of the frozen ZTF pipeline,” not “independent catalogs” or “independent validation datasets.” Freeze crossmatches and all ambiguity resolution before opening ZTF outcomes.
--
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-182-    27	   **Fix:** derive the formula using the actual integration time, distinguish Nyquist aliasing from boxcar attenuation, and test it numerically at the null, Nyquist period, and threshold.
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-183-    28	
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-184-    29	5. **REJECT-LEVEL — The D2 phases are unspecified and potentially artificial.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-185-    30	   The Romero tables provide periods and amplitudes, not the phases needed to reconstruct a unique waveform. “Shared \(t_{\rm ref}\)” secures cross-band coherence but may align all modes at one arbitrary phase. Sparse ZTF recovery can depend strongly on phase and multimode interference. DAV amplitudes also vary between the TESS and ZTF epochs.  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:186:    31	   **Fix:** assign independent prespecified random phases per mode, share each mode’s phase across bands, use multiple phase draws, and include temporal-amplitude scaling as a sensitivity axis. Inference must cluster repeated realizations by source.
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-187-    32	
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-188-    33	6. **REJECT-LEVEL — Real timestamps and residuals do not imply real-sky completeness.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-189-    34	   D2 preserves selected timestamps, errors, and residual artifacts. It does not preserve the joint distribution of target position, detector, color, blending, crowding, crossmatch failures, source extraction, quality cuts, native variability, or survey availability. Because injection occurs after at least some upstream operations, it cannot validate those operations.  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-190-    35	   **Fix:** call the result “conditional injection–recovery efficiency of the search stage.” An end-to-end claim requires injection upstream of extraction/QC or real labeled ZTF targets followed through every pipeline stage.
--
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-192-    37	7. **MAJOR — Arm-A nulls measure a model false-alarm probability, not real-sky FPR.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-193-    38	   Gaussian draws on real timestamps test calibration under Gaussian noise and the chosen error model. They omit non-Gaussian artifacts, blending, calibration failures, and intrinsic variability.  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-194-    39	   **Fix:** label this “Gaussian-null false-alarm rate.” A real-sky FPR requires independently identified quiet sources processed end to end.
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-195-    40	
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:196:    41	8. **MAJOR — D2’s repeated injections invalidate ordinary Wilson intervals.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:197:    42	   Three windows per Romero target, multiple phases, and 18 transformation variants are correlated replicates. Treating them as independent Bernoulli trials produces overconfident intervals.  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:198:    43	   **Fix:** specify the target-level estimand and use a two-stage or cross-classified bootstrap over Romero sources and template windows. Report the number of unique sources and windows separately.
