generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-258-   103	20. **REJECT-LEVEL — The three datasets cannot be collapsed into one selection-function measurement.**  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err:259:   104	    D1 is 19 labeled white dwarfs, D2 is a conditional synthetic DAV experiment, and D3 is a magnitude-truncated Kepler-field δ-Scuti sample. They have different populations, labels, amplitudes, windows, and endpoints. The [slip rule](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md:176) claiming D2+D1 alone “flips” the independent-label condition is untenable.  
generalization/reviews/G2/sol_referee2.err-260-   105	    **Fix:** report three separate response assessments. Any synthesis must be qualitative or list domain-specific estimands side by side—never pool them into “the pipeline selection function.”
