generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-5-The decisive problems occur in the [D3 design](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md:75), [D2 design](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md:103), and [headline estimands](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:38).
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-6-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-7-## Numbered objections
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-8-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:9:1. **REJECT-LEVEL — D2 templates are selected using the pipeline outcome being evaluated.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:10:   The templates are the 510 stars previously classified as “not detected” by the frozen pipeline. That is a direct circularity path: the evaluation conditions the real-noise/window population on the algorithm having failed to trigger. This suppresses trigger-prone artifacts and selects favorable noise realizations. The admission that arm-B nulls are tautological does not cure the bias in positive injection recovery.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:11:   **Fix:** draw templates without reference to frozen-pipeline status—ideally the actual ZTF windows of the Romero targets, otherwise a prespecified random or weighted sample of the full parent population. Run paired zero-signal and injected versions. If unchanged, every D2 result must explicitly be conditional on “previously non-triggering templates.”
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-12-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-13-2. **MAJOR — D3 has no obvious ZTF label leakage, but “independently labeled” needs qualification.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-14-   Murphy labels and Mo frequencies are external to the ZTF pipeline, so I see no direct D3 label-to-ZTF-output circularity. However, Mo is described as a Murphy×Bowman-derived sample; these are not independent label sources.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-15-   **Fix:** say “labels obtained independently of the frozen ZTF pipeline,” not “independent catalogs” or “independent validation datasets.” Freeze crossmatches and all ambiguity resolution before opening ZTF outcomes.
--
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-27-   **Fix:** derive the formula using the actual integration time, distinguish Nyquist aliasing from boxcar attenuation, and test it numerically at the null, Nyquist period, and threshold.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-28-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-29-5. **REJECT-LEVEL — The D2 phases are unspecified and potentially artificial.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-30-   The Romero tables provide periods and amplitudes, not the phases needed to reconstruct a unique waveform. “Shared \(t_{\rm ref}\)” secures cross-band coherence but may align all modes at one arbitrary phase. Sparse ZTF recovery can depend strongly on phase and multimode interference. DAV amplitudes also vary between the TESS and ZTF epochs.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:31:   **Fix:** assign independent prespecified random phases per mode, share each mode’s phase across bands, use multiple phase draws, and include temporal-amplitude scaling as a sensitivity axis. Inference must cluster repeated realizations by source.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-32-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-33-6. **REJECT-LEVEL — Real timestamps and residuals do not imply real-sky completeness.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-34-   D2 preserves selected timestamps, errors, and residual artifacts. It does not preserve the joint distribution of target position, detector, color, blending, crowding, crossmatch failures, source extraction, quality cuts, native variability, or survey availability. Because injection occurs after at least some upstream operations, it cannot validate those operations.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-35-   **Fix:** call the result “conditional injection–recovery efficiency of the search stage.” An end-to-end claim requires injection upstream of extraction/QC or real labeled ZTF targets followed through every pipeline stage.
--
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-37-7. **MAJOR — Arm-A nulls measure a model false-alarm probability, not real-sky FPR.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-38-   Gaussian draws on real timestamps test calibration under Gaussian noise and the chosen error model. They omit non-Gaussian artifacts, blending, calibration failures, and intrinsic variability.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-39-   **Fix:** label this “Gaussian-null false-alarm rate.” A real-sky FPR requires independently identified quiet sources processed end to end.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-40-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:41:8. **MAJOR — D2’s repeated injections invalidate ordinary Wilson intervals.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:42:   Three windows per Romero target, multiple phases, and 18 transformation variants are correlated replicates. Treating them as independent Bernoulli trials produces overconfident intervals.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:43:   **Fix:** specify the target-level estimand and use a two-stage or cross-classified bootstrap over Romero sources and template windows. Report the number of unique sources and windows separately.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-44-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-45-9. **REJECT-LEVEL — `dSct=0` does not support the claimed FPR, including as an “upper bound.”**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-46-   These objects may be other real variables or missed δ-Scuti stars. A legitimate detection of another variable is not a false positive for a generic variability pipeline. Moreover,
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-47-   \[
--
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-50-   is not necessarily an upper bound on \(P(D\mid C)\) without an unjustified ordering assumption.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-51-   **Fix:** rename it “trigger rate among Murphy non-dSct stars.” For FPR, construct an independently selected Kepler-quiet control set and audit detected controls for contamination and crossmatch failures.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-52-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-53-10. **MAJOR — Matching any Mo frequency creates a multiple-opportunity match.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:54:    The Mo table contains roughly 141 frequencies per cataloged star on average. A candidate matched to any listed frequency has many chances to succeed by accident, especially around window aliases. Calling this `matched_primary` is misleading.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-55-    **Fix:** make dominant-mode recovery the primary frequency metric; retain any-published-mode recovery as secondary. Estimate accidental-match probability by permuting frequency lists between stars or shifting them while preserving mode count and frequency support.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-56-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-57-11. **REJECT-LEVEL — The 456/610 amplitude join can bias the headline turn-on curve.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-58-    The amplitude estimand is
--
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-92-    \(P(\text{frequency match}\mid\text{detected, labeled positive})\) is frequency agreement among known positives. It is not positive predictive value. The roster’s altered prevalence and contaminated negative class make population purity unidentified.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-93-    **Fix:** rename it “frequency-match fraction among detected positives.” Claim purity only after representative prevalence weighting and adjudication of detections in a valid negative population.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-94-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-95-18. **MAJOR — The turn-on analysis is insufficiently prespecified.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:96:    Exact bin edges, minimum cell sizes, treatment of empty/sparse cells, and any smoothing or monotonic fitting are absent. A min–max band across transformation ladders is a sensitivity envelope, not statistical uncertainty.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-97-    **Fix:** freeze bin edges and minimum counts now; distinguish sampling intervals from model-sensitivity envelopes; use cluster-aware intervals for D2.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-98-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-99-19. **MAJOR — McNemar does not by itself establish “complementarity.”**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-100-    The L-S side requires frequency truth while the census side does not, so the paired outcomes are not symmetric. McNemar tests marginal discordance, not scientific complementarity or incremental recovery.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-101-    **Fix:** headline the full overlap table and incremental completeness with paired confidence intervals. Treat McNemar as a secondary comparison using genuinely parallel detection definitions.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-102-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-103-20. **REJECT-LEVEL — The three datasets cannot be collapsed into one selection-function measurement.**  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:104:    D1 is 19 labeled white dwarfs, D2 is a conditional synthetic DAV experiment, and D3 is a magnitude-truncated Kepler-field δ-Scuti sample. They have different populations, labels, amplitudes, windows, and endpoints. The [slip rule](/Users/jackneo/Documents/vonhippel-base9/astro-wd/generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md:176) claiming D2+D1 alone “flips” the independent-label condition is untenable.  
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-105-    **Fix:** report three separate response assessments. Any synthesis must be qualitative or list domain-specific estimands side by side—never pool them into “the pipeline selection function.”
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-106-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-107-## Wording that could survive review
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-108-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-109-If the D2 design remains unchanged:
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-110-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md:111:> Using published TESS mode solutions as external signal prescriptions, we measured the frozen search’s conditional injection–recovery efficiency after adding synthetic DAV signals to previously non-triggering ZTF light curves. This semi-empirical test preserves the timestamps and residuals of the selected templates but remains conditional on template selection, phase and stationarity assumptions, the TESS-to-ZTF amplitude transformation, and successful upstream data processing. It is not an empirical estimate of DAV completeness on the ZTF sky.
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-112-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-113-For D3:
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-114-
generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.md-115-> We measured detection completeness in Murphy et al. dSct=1 stars satisfying \(g\ge13.2\). Amplitude-dependent results are conditional on the 456/610 objects joined to Mo et al. and use historical Kepler-band amplitudes. The trigger rate among dSct=0 stars is reported as a negative-class trigger rate, not as a constant-source false-positive rate.
--
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-1-#!/usr/bin/env python3
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:2:"""Synthesize D2 exposure shards: DAV truth signals in real ZTF windows.
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-3-
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-4-Template pool: ALL 928 stars of the published 2026-08-01 catalog — NOT the
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:5:510 not-detected subset (G1 referee finding 1: conditioning templates on the
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-6-pipeline's own non-detection is a circularity path). Native variability is
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-7-handled by frequency-matched scoring plus paired controls. Every shard
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:8:preserves the template's real epochs (bjd_tdb), real cadence structure and
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-9-real magerr; arms differ in what carries the noise:
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-10-
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:11:  arm B (92…)  signal added to the REAL ZTF magnitudes — the headline arm
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-12-               ("TESS-truth signals injected into real ZTF photometry").
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:13:  ctrl (95…)   paired uninjected copy of every unique arm-B template window —
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:14:               identifies windows that trigger natively (real variables in
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-15-               the pool), so injected-recovery is scored against its own
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:16:               window's baseline behavior.
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-17-  arm A (93…)  signal added to a synthetic Gaussian floor (median mag +
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:18:               N(0, magerr_i)) — diagnostic; separates window effects from
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-19-               real-noise effects.
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-20-  nulls (94…)  arm-A construction with amplitude_scale = 0 — 1,000 shards
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:21:               cycling the 928 windows with distinct noise seeds (windows
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-22-               repeat, noise does not). This measures the GAUSSIAN-NULL
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-23-               false-alarm rate, not a real-sky FPR (G1 stats finding 11).
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-24-
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-25-Template matching per target: |median zg mag − target G| <= 0.25 (widened to
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-26-0.5, then nearest-K, when the pool is thin — flagged in the manifest);
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:27:K=3 at the 10/50/90th percentiles of median-exposures-per-night, because 75%
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-28-of zg nights are single-exposure and per-night median subtraction is the
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-29-pre-registered dominant penalty (plan risk 3).
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-30-
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-31-Run matrix (plan): nominal (1.7, 0.80) on K=3 for arms A+B; the other 8
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:32:ladder points on the median template only; 1,000 nulls.
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-33-
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-34-Campaign id layout (19 digits): AA TTTTTTTTTT K GR 0000
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:35:  AA arm prefix (92/93), T zero-padded TIC, K template index (0/1/2),
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py:36:  G/R ladder indices (1-3) into {1.4,1.7,2.1} x {0.70,0.80,0.90}, 22=nominal.
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-37-  Nulls: 94 + 17-digit serial. Full mapping in shard_manifest.csv.
scripts/generalization/build_d2_shards.py-38-"""
