generalization/reviews/G1/sol_referee.err:16:You are a hostile AAS/MNRAS referee reviewing a campaign DESIGN before execution. Read generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md and generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md in this repo. Attack: (1) label independence claims for D2 (TESS-truth transplant) and D3 (Kepler dSct x ZTF) — is there ANY circularity path? (2) whether D2 'truth model injected into real windows' can support completeness claims about the pipeline on real sky, and exactly how the writeup must be phrased to survive review; (3) whether D3's dSct=0 negatives support an FPR claim; (4) selection effects introduced by the g>=13.2 cut and the Mo+2026 amplitude join (456/610 positives have amplitudes — does conditioning on the join bias the turn-on curve?); (5) anything that would make you reject an abstract claiming a 'quantified selection-function measurement'. Be specific and ruthless; number every objection; for each, say REJECT-LEVEL, MAJOR, or MINOR, and what fix would satisfy you.
