generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-238-2. D3 completeness ≈ 0 below the a95 floor → stratification IS the
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-239-   deliverable (turn-on curve).
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-240-3. D2 high-pass ≈ 0 from the single-exposure-night penalty → pre-registered
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-241-   expected headline, stratified to be explanatory.
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md:242:4. A_r/A_g lever → mandatory ladder; headline reported as a band.
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-243-5. D3 negatives not constants → FPR an upper bound, stated.
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-244-6. Desktop unreachable → D2 on laptop after D3 (+1 day).
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-245-7. Romero mode tables are LaTeX prose with typos (comma decimals, stray
generalization/GENERALIZATION_PLAN.md-246-   units) → parser with hard row-count and range asserts; G3 reviews the
--
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-24-  denominators (both conditional on scorable/S_p = 1).
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-25-- **correct-frequency fraction among detected positives** — what an earlier
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-26-  draft called "purity"; it is not positive predictive value and is never
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-27-  labeled purity. Class-level PPV is reported for D3 only, with sampling
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:28:  weights (negatives carry weight pool/sample = 7292/2314), as a
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-29-  prevalence-weighted estimate with the contaminated-negative caveat.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-30-- **negative-class trigger rate** — P(rule fires | Murphy dSct=0). NOT called
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-31-  FPR: the class contains non-dSct variables; reported with sampling weights
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-32-  and, after adjudication of triggered negatives (W4), split into
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-33-  "plausible real variable" vs "unexplained".
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-34-- **Gaussian-null false-alarm rate (FPR_Gaussian)** — P(confirmed | arm-A
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:35:  zero-amplitude null), n = 1000 over the 928-window frame (windows repeat,
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-36-  seeds do not). Acceptance criterion (preregistered): one-sided 95% upper
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-37-  bound <= 0.5% at zero events. The FP frequency-distribution/alias audit is
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-38-  descriptive only below 10 events.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:39:- **native trigger rate of the template pool** — P(confirmed | paired
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:40:  uninjected control window), the 95-prefix arm. Context for D2 recovery,
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-41-  not an FPR.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-42-
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-43-## Frequency-match taxonomy (disjoint labels, strict first)
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-44-
--
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-47-(D3: Mo frequencies for that KIC; D2: injected modes):
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-48-
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-49-1. `direct` — within tolerance of a truth frequency;
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-50-2. `harmonic` — within tolerance of 2f or f/2 of a truth frequency;
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:51:3. `window_alias` — within tolerance of |f_truth ± k f_sid|, k = 1, 2
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-52-   (sidereal-day family, the pipeline's own alias model);
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:53:4. `ambiguous` — matches >1 truth frequency class above;
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-54-5. `unmatched`.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-55-
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-56-Headline frequency recovery counts `direct` only, scored against the
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:57:pipeline's BEST candidate (`matched_primary`). D3's primary truth frequency
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-58-is the DOMINANT Mo mode; any-mode direct matches are a secondary column.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-59-`matched_any_mode` over the 15 stored top_peaks is diagnostic only.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-60-Chance-match calibration: truth lists permuted across stars (frozen seed,
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-61-100 permutations) → accidental direct-match rate reported beside every
--
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-65-
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-66-1. `confirmed` (headline), 2. `confirmed|candidate`, 3. `census`
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-67-(any of six frozen ratios >= 2.5), 4. `either` (1 OR 3).
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-68-Primary claim family (preregistered): rule 1, pass = best of {low, high}
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:69:(the frozen `overall_result` ordering), nominal D2 variant (1.7/0.80,
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:70:de-dilution off, arm B), per dataset. Everything else is labeled a
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-71-pointwise descriptive sensitivity analysis; no simultaneous-coverage claim.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-72-
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-73-## Units of analysis and intervals
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-74-
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:75:- D1/D3: the star is the unit; Wilson 95% intervals on independent per-star
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:76:  proportions; weighted estimates use the effective-sample-size Wilson
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-77-  approximation.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:78:- D2: the TESS target is the CLUSTER. K=3 template windows and ladder/phase
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-79-  variants are correlated replicates, never pooled as independent trials.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:80:  Per-stratum (10/50/90th percentile window) proportions are reported
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-81-  separately; aggregates are equal-weight standardized means over targets
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:82:  with cluster bootstrap intervals (resample targets, keep all replicates;
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-83-  B = 2000, frozen seed). Ladder results: nominal is primary; the min-max
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-84-  across the 3x3 grid is a "prespecified finite-grid sensitivity range",
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-85-  never a confidence band; endpoint scenarios identified.
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-86-
--
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-89-Primary table (per dataset, on labeled positives with both methods
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-90-available): C = census flag; L = rule-1 detection (detection-only, no
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-91-frequency requirement — symmetric margins). Report the full 2x2, both
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-92-discordant fractions, union completeness, and incremental yields
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md:93:P(C=1,L=0), P(C=0,L=1) with intervals (Wilson for D3/D1; cluster bootstrap
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-94-for D2). Exact McNemar is SECONDARY (marginal-homogeneity only; it does not
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-95-measure complementarity).
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-96-
generalization/METRICS_SPEC.md-97-## Surfaces
